[2026-03-15T09:00:07.202Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P1YKFhsUevNBW53D6EJnom","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Install globally:**\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n**Authenticate:** Create an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and set the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Main Commands\n\n- **`record [url]`** – Launch Replay Browser and start recording (defaults to `about:blank`)\n- **`upload [ids...]`** – Upload recordings; without IDs opens interactive selection\n- **`list`** – Display all local recordings with details\n- **`remove [ids...]`** – Delete recordings; use `-a/--all` for everything\n- **`login/logout`** – Manage account authentication\n- **`info`** – Show CLI version and browser details\n- **`upload-source-maps`** – Upload source maps with options for grouping and filtering\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n1. Record a session: `replayio record https://myapp.com`\n2. Upload when ready: `replayio upload <recording-id>`\n3. Access the recording URL provided after upload\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for additional details. The CLI also includes an MCP server integration for Claude-based debugging of recorded applications."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb525227-e996-4510-92e8-ef0d46b50769","uuid":"f3734186-a445-4a29-9066-f9372cfb057e","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Reference\n\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Here's what you need to know:\n\n## Quick Start\n\n**Install globally:**\n```sh\nnpm i -g replayio\n```\n\n**Authenticate:** Create an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and set the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Main Commands\n\n- **`record [url]`** – Launch Replay Browser and start recording (defaults to `about:blank`)\n- **`upload [ids...]`** – Upload recordings; without IDs opens interactive selection\n- **`list`** – Display all local recordings with details\n- **`remove [ids...]`** – Delete recordings; use `-a/--all` for everything\n- **`login/logout`** – Manage account authentication\n- **`info`** – Show CLI version and browser details\n- **`upload-source-maps`** – Upload source maps with options for grouping and filtering\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n1. Record a session: `replayio record https://myapp.com`\n2. Upload when ready: `replayio upload <recording-id>`\n3. Access the recording URL provided after upload\n\nUse `-h` or `--help` with any command for additional details. The CLI also includes an MCP server integration for Claude-based debugging of recorded applications.","durationMs":3643,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T09:00:08.071Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LxCSKugqQPRZZnfH8xV3yj","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview Document\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for investigating Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser session data. Here's the core content:\n\n**Purpose**: \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**Key Concept**: The recordings function as comprehensive databases documenting all execution events, allowing investigators to explore application behavior systematically.\n\n**Investigation Methodology** (4 steps):\n1. Frame investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form and support hypotheses with gathered evidence\n\n**Core Terms**:\n- **Point**: Unique execution moment when JS statements run or significant state-affecting events occur\n- **Element**: DOM element reference independent of specific points\n\n**Tool Categories**:\n\n*Exploratory Tools* discover what happened:\n- Errors (UncaughtException, ReactException)\n- Timeline data (ConsoleMessages, LocalStorage, NetworkRequest, ReactRenders)\n- Source analysis (ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources)\n\n*Explanatory Tools* clarify causation:\n- Dependencies (GetStack, ControlDependency)\n- Details (DescribePoint, InspectElement, ReactComponents, Logpoint, Evaluate)\n\n**Key Recommendations**: Locate relevant code, verify execution, examine variable states using Logpoint, and employ ControlDependency for timing analysis."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb525227-e996-4510-92e8-ef0d46b50769","uuid":"d08189d0-dd40-4763-a1e1-b41b80420852","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview Document\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for investigating Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser session data. Here's the core content:\n\n**Purpose**: \"Use Replay MCP to inspect the contents of https://replay.io recordings.\"\n\n**Key Concept**: The recordings function as comprehensive databases documenting all execution events, allowing investigators to explore application behavior systematically.\n\n**Investigation Methodology** (4 steps):\n1. Frame investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form and support hypotheses with gathered evidence\n\n**Core Terms**:\n- **Point**: Unique execution moment when JS statements run or significant state-affecting events occur\n- **Element**: DOM element reference independent of specific points\n\n**Tool Categories**:\n\n*Exploratory Tools* discover what happened:\n- Errors (UncaughtException, ReactException)\n- Timeline data (ConsoleMessages, LocalStorage, NetworkRequest, ReactRenders)\n- Source analysis (ListSources, ReadSource, SearchSources)\n\n*Explanatory Tools* clarify causation:\n- Dependencies (GetStack, ControlDependency)\n- Details (DescribePoint, InspectElement, ReactComponents, Logpoint, Evaluate)\n\n**Key Recommendations**: Locate relevant code, verify execution, examine variable states using Logpoint, and employ ControlDependency for timing analysis.","durationMs":3616,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
