wn {\n  position: absolute;\n  top: 100%;\n  left: 0;\n  z-index: 100;\n  min-width: 280px;\n  background: var(--color-surface);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  box-shadow: 0 2px 8px var(--color-shadow);\n  padding: 16px;\n  margin-top: 4px;\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__row {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: space-between;\n  padding: 8px 0;\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__row + .passenger-selector__row {\n  border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-light);\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__info {\n  display: flex;\n  flex-direction: column;\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__category {\n  font-size: 14px;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  color: var(--color-text-primary);\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__age {\n  font-size: 12px;\n  color: var(--color-text-secondary);\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__controls {\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  gap: 12px;\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__btn {\n  width: 32px;\n  height: 32px;\n  display: flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  border-radius: var(--radius-full);\n  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);\n  font-size: 16px;\n  color: var(--color-primary);\n  transition: background 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__btn:hover:not(:disabled) {\n  background: var(--color-primary-light);\n  border-color: var(--color-primary);\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__btn:disabled {\n  color: var(--color-border);\n  border-color: var(--color-border-light);\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n\n.passenger-selector__count {\n  font-size: 16px;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  min-width: 20px;\n  text-align: center;\n  color: var(--color-text-primary);\n}\n","numLines":108,"startLine":1,"totalLines":108}}}
[2026-03-15T09:09:59.289Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SsPtNtsYQ5vZbTUJbJ2D55","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is that when `PassengerCountSelector` is rendered with `initiallyOpen`, its dropdown uses `position: absolute` with `z-index: 100`. The dropdown extends beyond the container and overlaps the \"Done\" button. The passenger-selector__dropdown is positioned absolutely below the trigger, but since the entire PassengerCountSelector is inside the `search-summary-bar__editor`, the dropdown extends outside the editor.\n\nThe problem is that the PassengerCountSelector's dropdown is absolute-positioned and overlaps the Done button below it. Since the trigger button is still visible (even though the dropdown is already open), the trigger's row content is positioned between the Apply button and the actual dropdown contents.\n \nThe passenger row is intercepting pointer events on the Done button because the dropdown's absolute positioning places it on top of the button in the visual stack, even though the Done button comes after it in the DOM. I need to either prevent the dropdown from being rendered inside the editor container or adjust the positioning so it doesn't overlap interactive elements.\n\nThe simplest solution is to render the passenger selector content inline without absolute positioning when it's already inside an editor popup, rather than trying to manage z-index conflicts. I'll modify the component to detect when it's being used inline and render the dropdown content directly without the wrapper's absolute positioning.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2662,"cache_read_input_tokens":62061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2662,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb525227-e996-4510-92e8-ef0d46b50769","uuid":"231b7820-e9b3-477d-af22-57054c95c428"}
